    {
      "id": "a6275027-01d3-4a75-9144-9d79d9cc07c4",
      "name": "📌 Overview – How This Workflow Works",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -4144,
        2816
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 2,
        "width": 948,
        "height": 980,
        "content": "## 🧠 Smart AI Second Brain – Auto-Summarize, Categorize & Prioritize Content\n\n### How it works\nThis workflow builds a personal, self-organising knowledge base from THREE content streams. **RSS:** a daily schedule reads configured feeds. **Email:** a Gmail trigger fires on new newsletters. **YouTube (new):** send any YouTube link to your Telegram bot and its transcript is pulled in too. All three are normalised into one format, merged, deduplicated against your Google Sheets Second Brain, and filtered for empty content.\n\nRelevant items then go through TWO AI passes: (1) a relevance filter, then (2) a categorize-and-prioritize pass that tags a topic category and a 1-10 importance score. A third AI call writes the summary, key insights, and tags, and a lightweight related-items lookup links each new entry back to similar past entries already in your Second Brain.\n\nEach entry is logged to both a per-category sheet tab AND a master log. High-priority items (8+) trigger an immediate Telegram alert; everything else is silently queued and rolled up into an automatic weekly digest so you aren't pinged for every minor article. Optional (disabled-by-default) nodes let you mirror entries into Notion or spin up Todoist action items without forking the template.\n\n### Setup steps\n1. Update `Set RSS Feed URLs` with the feeds you want to follow.\n2. Connect **Gmail OAuth2** to the Newsletter Email Trigger.\n3. Connect **Telegram Bot API** to both Telegram trigger nodes and all Telegram send nodes.\n4. Connect **OpenAI API** to all three AI nodes (Relevance Filter, Categorize & Prioritize, Summarize, Weekly Roundup).\n5. Connect **Google Sheets OAuth2** to every Sheets node — replace `REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_GOOGLE_SHEET_ID`, and create tabs named `All Entries` plus one per category.\n6. In `Map Category to Sheet Tab`, replace the placeholder GIDs with your real tab IDs (Sheet tab → right-click → Copy link → the number after `gid=`).\n7. Replace `REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_TRANSCRIPT_API` in `Fetch Video Transcript` with your preferred YouTube-transcript service.\n8. Connect **Slack OAuth2** to the error alert node — set your ops channel ID.\n9. Optionally enable and wire up `Export to Notion` and/or `Create Todoist Action Item` with your own credentials.\n10. Activate all triggers (Daily Schedule, Gmail, Telegram, Weekly Schedule)."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "2b4cb2de-e7a7-4d41-ad82-aa6a1adc27c3",
      "name": "Section – Dual Content Intake",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1696,
        3200
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1256,
        "height": 904,
        "content": "## 📡 Dual Content Intake (RSS + Email)\nTwo parallel triggers feed the same pipeline. The daily schedule reads configured RSS feeds and normalises each article. The Gmail trigger fires on new newsletters, strips HTML, and normalises the email body. Both produce identical structured objects before merging. See the separate YouTube Link Intake section below for the third source."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "d17b22da-f370-4be7-904e-a065b4091be6",
      "name": "Section – Deduplication & Relevance Filter",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -384,
        3520
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1404,
        "height": 808,
        "content": "## 🔍 Deduplication & Relevance Filter\nFetches all existing links from Google Sheets to detect duplicates — items already in your Second Brain are silently skipped. Remaining items pass through a GPT-4o-mini relevance check. Off-topic or low-quality content is dropped before the expensive summarisation step."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "6efe5200-293c-40d0-a1e9-43f5e746b754",
      "name": "Section – AI Summarization & Second Brain Logging",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1136,
        3360
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 2052,
        "height": 892,
        "content": "## 🗂️➡️✍️ Categorize, Prioritize, Summarize & Log\nRelevant items are first classified into a topic category and given a 1-10 importance score, then summarised by GPT-4o-mini into a structured JSON (title, summary, key insights, tags). A related-items lookup links each entry to similar past entries. Everything is logged to a per-category sheet tab AND a master log; high-priority items also get an immediate Telegram alert."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "060d7e01-a1b2-4e68-adac-1ab6e21367e3",
      "name": "🔑 Credentials & Configuration",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1104,
        4544
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 508,
        "height": 524,
        "content": "## 🔑 Credentials Required\n- **Gmail OAuth2** — newsletter email trigger\n- **Telegram Bot API** — YouTube link command, acknowledgement reply, immediate alerts, weekly roundup, error alert\n- **OpenAI API** — relevance filter, categorize/prioritize, summarization, weekly roundup\n- **Google Sheets OAuth2** — dedup check, per-category logging, master log, weekly digest read\n- **Slack OAuth2** — error alert channel\n- *Optional:* **Notion API** — only if you enable the Notion export node\n- *Optional:* **Todoist API** — only if you enable the Todoist action-item node\n- *Optional:* a transcript-fetching API/key for the `Fetch Video Transcript` node\n\nNever hardcode API keys or personal IDs in shared templates."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
